    "updated_at": "2026-06-14T03:08:03Z",
    "body": "Thanks! Just getting around to taking a look at this -\r\n\r\nRegarding the raycast.html example changes: I think adding separate dedicated culling in the example itself misrepresents the benefits of library a bit. The goal of the example is to show what the improvements are over just using the built-in three.js raycasting without any other user-land changes. There may be some benefit in adding a sphere check to the `MeshBVH.raycastObject3D` function, instead, but ultimately I think the \"ObjectBVH\" is a better solution for something like this, which we have other examples for.\r\n\r\nOn the WGSL changes - I'm currently working through adding an improved method for building TSL nodes for compute queries (see #881) so the current notes will be removed in some upcoming releases (in fact they weren't even working correctly on most platforms 😅 see #832). It looks like there are some good changes here, though - the distance-based culling for the bounds and triangles in particular seem good. I'll plan to update the examples in #881, as well, and if you'd like to try these changes in the new implementation afterward that would be great. Otherwise I try them when I have a chance!",
